# Landing Page Maintenance

When adding a **new user-facing feature** (type `"feature"` in release notes), evaluate whether it should appear on the landing page at `src/app/landing/page.tsx`.

## When to Update

Update the landing page when the new feature:

- Is a top-level capability visible to customers (e.g. new dashboard section, new tool, new data source)
- Strengthens the Free-to-Pro value proposition
- Would be compelling to investors or potential users on first impression

Do **not** update for internal improvements, minor fixes, or backend-only changes.

## What to Update

1. **FEATURES array** — add or update entries in the `FEATURES` constant with `title`, `description`, `screenshot`, and optional `badge` ("Pro").
2. **Feature card grid** — if the feature deserves a quick summary card (6-card grid below the main features), add or replace a card.
3. **Pricing tier lists** — if the feature changes what Free or Pro includes, update the `PRICING` tiers.
4. **Screenshot** — take a new screenshot with `browser_take_screenshot` and save it to `public/screenshots/`. Use `1280x800` resolution.

## Screenshot Conventions

- Save to `public/screenshots/<feature-slug>.png`
- Use the dark theme for consistency
- Reference via `/screenshots/<feature-slug>.png` in the `FEATURES` array

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Feature title and description are clear and benefit-oriented
- [ ] Screenshot is high-quality and shows the feature in context
- [ ] Pro features include the `badge: "Pro"` property
- [ ] Pricing lists stay accurate with current tier structure
